On Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:02:33 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> Is it necessary to match the cur/ new/ tmp/ structure? I would think
> it's fine to move it straight to archive/.

No. notmuch indexes any file under the database root, maildir or not,
and with maildir.synchronize_flags off nothing reads which maildir
subdirectory a file is in. The path:archive/** rule in "[PATCH v2 1/2]
notmuch: Tag messages under archive/ as archived" [1] matches a flat
archive/ just as it did archive/cur/.

> That would also simplify the logic quite a bit I think. Just get the
> list of files, and move them all into archive/.

Done that way: mkdir -p, then a notmuch search for the files of
messages tagged archive and not already under archive/, an mv of each
into maildir/archive/, and notmuch new. The check for cur/ or new/ is
gone too, since the list has no other directory a message could be in.
The recipe is down from 16 lines to 11. It is posted as "[PATCH v2]
mail: Add just archive" [2].

One doc follows from this. "[PATCH v2 2/2] zib: Patch review
workflow - Archiving mail" [3] says the moderator moves files to
maildir/archive/cur/. If you take the flat layout I will send a v3
that drops the cur/.

Thanks for the review.

